# Copy to .env.local and fill in — see FORKING.md step 3.
# Both values come from the Supabase dashboard: Settings → API.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix means Next.js inlines these into the browser
# bundle at build time — that's fine here, the anon key is designed
# to be public and is governed entirely by RLS.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# NOT read by the app itself, for anything — not the public site, not
# the studio, not the cron route (which deliberately uses the anon
# key; see src/app/api/cron/keep-warm/route.ts for why). Only used as
# a one-off terminal env var for the local verification scripts in
# FORKING.md step 3. Never put this in .env.local for local dev unless
# you're running those scripts; it bypasses RLS entirely.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Vercel-only. Add this env var to the Vercel project (Settings →
# Environment Variables) — a random string, 16+ characters, e.g. from
# a password generator. Vercel does NOT generate this for you; you
# set it (verified against Vercel's own cron-jobs docs before writing
# this). Once set, Vercel automatically sends it as the Authorization
# header on every cron invocation of /api/cron/keep-warm — that's what
# the route checks against.
# CRON_SECRET=
